{"author":{"id":"1949ffc23f11a8cb4f8c42a45c9ad241b49570df9a18687489e9ea78d87c54a3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1779385836,"nonce":"VRJEv1OCr168aHQg111FRk2o0eE=","title":"Studio Workspace runtime playback and validation overlays","message":"## Problem\n\nThe Workspace projection should eventually be useful not only for authoring tasks/mechanics/objectives, but also for inspecting what actually happens during training, validation, and evaluation. That is related to the Workspace spatial representation contract, but it has different data dependencies: checkpoints, rollouts, validation jobs, artifacts, live or periodic status, and provider/execution manifests.\n\nThis issue tracks runtime playback and validation overlays for the Workspace tab. It should share spatial entity ids, coordinate frames, and representation metadata with `946c859`, but it should not block the first authoring representation slice.\n\n## Desired User Experience\n\nWhen training or evaluation is running, or when completed runs/evals have artifacts, Workspace should be able to switch from pure authoring/schematic mode into a contextual playback/inspection mode. Examples:\n\n- play a validation reach over the authored task/mechanics geometry;\n- show actual effector/arm trajectories against target/goal representations;\n- inspect whether a controller reaches, freezes, overshoots, oscillates, or ignores task targets;\n- overlay perturbations, cues, task phases, and objective windows where relevant;\n- compare training/eval conditions or checkpoints when the data is available;\n- make clear whether the view is showing authored intent, a sampled task instance, a validation rollout, an imported legacy trajectory, or a live/periodic training snapshot.\n\nThe shift between authoring and playback should be stateful and explainable: selected pipeline stage, selected run/eval/artifact, and available provider outputs determine what is shown.\n\n## Data and Execution Requirements\n\nThis depends on provider/execution surfaces, not only frontend rendering:\n\n- execution or validation jobs must emit or stream trajectory/rollout artifacts with enough metadata to map them into Workspace coordinates;\n- training can optionally download or materialize checkpoints at intervals, then run local or remote validation tasks to produce representative rollouts;\n- evaluation artifacts should carry task/mechanics/spec snapshot references so Workspace can replay them over the correct geometry;\n- manifests should record which spec snapshot, checkpoint, task variant, seed, and provider environment produced the trajectory;\n- missing or imported-only metadata should be represented honestly.\n\nThis intersects the live execution children that still need to be split from closed `c6b1b73`: generic SSH runner, RunPod/Modal adapters, log/status streaming, artifact sync, environment provenance, and manifest finalization.\n\n## Visual Modes\n\nExpected modes include:\n\n- authoring schematic: editable task/mechanics/objective entities from `946c859`;\n- sampled preview: generated task samples without a trained controller, useful for distributions and schedules;\n- validation playback: rollout from a checkpoint or current model against a selected task/eval condition;\n- evaluation playback: replay of completed evaluation artifacts;\n- live/progress overlay: periodic or streamed summary during training, probably lower fidelity than completed playback;\n- imported artifact view: best-effort rendering with explicit missing metadata warnings.\n\nThese modes should reuse the same entity ids and coordinate-frame metadata when possible, but they should be visibly distinct to avoid confusing authored intent with observed behavior.\n\n## Out of Scope\n\n- Designing the base Workspace spatial representation. That is `946c859`.\n- Implementing live cloud/worker execution. This issue consumes that capability once execution children exist.\n- Full video/animation production or report rendering. Report products should reference the same trajectory/figure artifacts through provider manifests.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Workspace can display at least one completed validation/evaluation trajectory over the authored task/mechanics representation.\n- The displayed trajectory is linked to a manifest/artifact/spec snapshot, not an untracked frontend blob.\n- The UI distinguishes authoring schematic mode from sampled-preview and runtime playback modes.\n- The provider artifact/manifest contract includes enough coordinate-frame/task/mechanics metadata for replay.\n- Missing metadata produces an explicit fallback state rather than misleading geometry.\n- The design cross-links to live execution, statistics/diagnostics, and analysis/report product issues.\n\n## Related Issues\n\n- `946c859` — Workspace spatial representation and objective authoring contract.\n- `a3e46d5` — product-depth and contract sequence umbrella.\n- `4178e12` — graph/spec worker lowering.\n- `c6c6da0` — provider/manifests/schema contract.\n- `f68cf66` — Feedbax as Mandible provider/plugin.\n- `e33f487` — manifests as canonical lineage with database indexing.\n- `d90b3e5` — training runs vs sessions/tabs.\n- `b2db05b`, `c722539`, `4cb86c8` — statistics/trajectory diagnostic surfaces, likely needing refresh under the pipeline/manifest model.\n- `e8452a4` — analysis layer migration and graph-step adapter.\n\n---\nCo-Authored-By: Codex (GPT-5) \u003ccodex@openai.com\u003e","files":null}]}